WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.800
He's been a musclebound military man with
biceps with size of Christmas hams.

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:08.780
He's served time in the Vietnam War and seen
things most could never imagine.

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:11.299
He was even a snake-seller in Thailand for
a while.

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:14.100
But now, John Rambo is a cowboy, baby.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:18.439
To celebrate the start of filming on Rambo
5, the upcoming installment in the action-packed

00:00:18.439 --> 00:00:23.690
Rambo franchise, series star Sylvester Stallone
shared two images of himself in character

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:24.180
as Rambo.

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:28.560
One might have expected to see the iconic
action hero standing shirtless in a jungle,

00:00:28.570 --> 00:00:33.400
wielding a massive weapon, sweating profusely,
and scowling at the camera in Rambo 5 – because,

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.340
you know, he's Rambo and that's who Rambo
is.

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:38.020
Or at least that's who he was.

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:43.480
In the first snap Stallone shared on his Instagram
account, his new cowboy-Rambo looks off camera

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:45.300
as he slips on a suede work glove.

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:46.680
In the caption, he wrote,

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:48.360
"Tonight we start filming…!"

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:52.660
While the first photo appears to have been
taken during a costume and makeup test shoot,

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:54.840
the second image was definitely taken on set.

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:59.540
Stallone is mounted on a dun-colored horse,
his head tilted down toward the forest floor.

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:05.180
Stallone captioned that snap, "Comes a Horseman
Wild and Free," a reference to Canadian singer-songwriter

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:08.320
Gordon Lightfoot's 1972 track "Don Quixote."

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:12.890
Confusing as the first-look photos may be,
there's actually a solid reason why Rambo

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:15.300
will look more like John Wayne in the new
Rambo.

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:19.500
The film will begin with Rambo living on his
father's ranch in Arizona the same one he

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:21.360
returned to at the end of Rambo 4.

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:26.380
According to Screen Daily, Rambo will go about
his everyday farm duties until he learns that

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:30.590
he must hunt down one of Mexico's deadliest,
most ruthless cartels who have kidnapped his

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:31.300
friend's daughter.

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:36.000
While some have found cowboy-hat-wearing Rambo
a bit strange, fans should thank their lucky

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:40.500
stars that they're even seeing snaps of Stallone
filming Rambo 5 in the first place, since

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:44.260
the actor was just a few years ago prepared
to say goodbye to Rambo for good.

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:50.140
In May 2010, Stallone told Empire that he
was, quote, "done [with Rambo]" and that he

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:53.850
was "99 percent sure" a fifth Rambo movie
wasn't going to happen.

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:55.760
"I think Rambo's pretty well done.

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:57.260
I don't think there'll be any more.

00:01:57.260 --> 00:02:00.960
[…] I feel that with Rocky Balboa, that
character came complete circle.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:01.660
He went home.

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:06.600
But for Rambo to go on another adventure might
be, I think, misinterpreted as a mercenary

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:08.040
gesture and not necessary."

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:12.660
At the time, he added that he was happy with
Rambo 4 and where his character's story ended,

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:17.470
due in large part to the fact that, as Stallone
put it, he "didn't pull any punches" while

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:19.840
writing the film's script or in directing
the movie.

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:20.700
He explained,

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.880
"I wanted it to be what civil war really is:
rough.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:25.160
You can't candy coat it.

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:26.680
And where do you go from there?"

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:29.700
Stallone apparently had a change of heart
shortly thereafter.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:35.180
In July 2010, he opened up during a fan Q&amp;A
session held on Ain't It Cool about what the

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:37.140
future held for the Rambo franchise.

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:41.620
Asked whether he would want to further explore
Rambo's back story, Stallone admitted that

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:45.740
he thought the possibility of a Rambo prequel
was "worth pondering," and that it would be

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:48.900
interesting for him to direct a new actor
as a younger Rambo.

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:49.840
He explained,

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:54.250
"The traumas, the loss and the tragedy of
being in Vietnam would certainly be a great

00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:58.450
challenge for a young actor, and it would
be ironic that Rambo directs younger Rambo

00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:00.200
having played it for 20 years plus."

00:03:00.550 --> 00:03:04.920
Obviously, all that thought turned into action,
and Stallone eventually agreed to starring

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:05.980
in a fifth Rambo movie.

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:10.500
Though he's traded in his signature bandana
and mullet for some new headgear, Rambo is

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:16.360
coming back in full force with a fresh aesthetic
to boot for Rambo 5, due out sometime in fall

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:16.990
2019.

